			"notes": "# Vintner 1.4.1 — Recipe Compatibility\n\nFor Minecraft 26.3 with Fabric Loader 0.19.5+, Fabric API 0.161.0+26.3 or compatible, Java 25+, and **ZenithGB Commons 0.1.2** (installed separately).\n\n## Fixed\n\n- Vanilla White Wool can again be crafted from four string without a Vineyard Netting collision.\n- The Soil Probe no longer conflicts with the vanilla Copper Shovel.\n- All 13 wood variants of the Fermentation Barrel no longer conflict with vanilla Chests.\n\n## Improved\n\n- The Soil Probe uses a clearer copper-tip and two-stick-handle pattern.\n- Fermentation Barrels use an open-top pattern of eight matching planks.\n- The Vintner's Almanac accepts any two red or white grapes, including two of the same colour.\n\nVineyard Netting now uses four string in the **four corners of a 3×3 crafting table** and still yields two nets. Existing ingredient costs, output quantities, public item and block IDs, and save data are unchanged. Back up your worlds before upgrading.\n\nThe separately reported Almanac display issue is still under investigation; this update does not claim to fix it.\n\nSHA-256 of `vintner-1.4.1-mc26.3-fabric.jar`:\n`b8ceb44489531767ea61d49a455a9ed3c2077194c33f8b5fff0cda149ecc5b8f`"
		},
